  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intel4Value &#x2013; Intelligent value chain management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will build an efficient, scalable and sustainable palm oil value chain between smallholder producers, providers, processors and consumers, creating a positive social impact on 2,857 workers (971 women), environmental protection of over 20,000 hectares and build a viable future for 1,200 (442 women) smallholder producers.The average size of a plantation is 10 ha. According to Fedepalma (branche organisation) a smallholder has less than 50 ha. In the scaling phase within the project area, it aims to reach another 1,300 smallholder producers.The project focuses on the development and implementation of a set of digital tools to support the transformation from standard production processes to sustainable production processes, and to create sustainability improvements along the palm oil value chain. The primary revenue model is therefore built around the development and implementation of the digital tools and the expected benefits they will generate in the long-term.The following digital tools are included in the project business case:&#x2022;	Farming solution;&#x2022;	Extension solution;&#x2022;	Agro-learning solution; and&#x2022;	Fintech solution (called &#x201c;Hola Prestamo&#x201d;).</narrative>
  </description>
